  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 140 PM CDT Tue Jun 23 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will continue to be the controlling feature \nfor our weather through the upcoming weekend. The ridge is \ncurrently centered near El Paso. As we move through this weekend \nand into next week, the ridge will gradually shift southward into \nnorth-central Mexico, while elongating/flattening, and expanding \neastward into the northern Gulf. And although the ridge will \nweaken somewhat during this time period, our temperatures will \nremain above normal, with average daily highs from the mid 90s to \naround 104. However, as the ridge maintains its presence over the \narea, heat will likely build over the area allowing afternoon \nhighs to warm a few degrees, with Friday and Saturday being our \nwarmest days. With highs potentially warming into the 105-110 \nrange from Thursday into Saturday across parts of the Big Country \nand western Concho Valley, we may need to issue Heat Advisories \nfor parts of the area.",
